  "pr_title": "docs(docs): add an illustrated how-to guide",
  "pr_description": "## Goal\n\nTeammates learn the setup and the daily workflow from a step-by-step guide. Each step has an animation that shows the step in Obsidian, SharePoint, Finder, Word, or System Settings.\n\n## Summary\n\n`docs/guide.md` describes nine steps: install the plugin with BRAT, sync a SharePoint library with OneDrive, find and open a document, edit and sync a note, add and reply to and resolve comments, send edits as tracked changes, resolve a `[!conflict]` callout, recognize locked content and keep private notes in `%% ... %%`, and fix setup problems with **Check setup**.\n\nEach step has a GIF in `docs/images/`. Each GIF has a static PNG of its final frame. The guide uses a `<picture>` element, so a reader with the reduced-motion setting sees the PNG.\n\nThe images are synthetic mockups, not screenshots. Command names, notices, sync results, callout formats, and Check setup results come from the plugin and the CLI code. The sample document is the \"Project plan\" document from `scripts/word_fixtures.py`. The images use sample names only (\"Alex Example\", \"Alice Smith\", \"Sam Lee\"), a sample site (\"Sample Team\" at `sample.sharepoint.com`), and a sample OneDrive folder (`OneDrive-SampleOrg`). The images contain no employer names and no work content.\n\nThe motion follows these rules: no animation for the command palette, because the keyboard opens it; 200 ms ease-out entrances for dialogs and notices, with faster exits; ease-in-out pointer movement; and a 50 ms stagger for the Check setup rows.\n\nThe README links to the guide from **Setup**. `CONTRIBUTING.md` lists `docs/` in the project structure table.\n\nThe images total about 10 MB. `09-check-setup.gif` is about 3.1 MB, and each of the other GIFs is from 0.5 MB to 1.2 MB. The tool that renders the images is not in this PR.\n\nThis change does not touch docx reading or patching.\n\n## Testing\n\nNo code changed, so the pre-commit hook skipped its checks. I checked the guide and the PR body for the em-dash and for curly quotation marks. I checked the frames of each animation against the command names and messages in `obsidian-plugin/main.ts`, `src/spsync/core.py`, `src/spsync/doctor.py`, and `src/spsync/patch/`.\n\nManual check: open `docs/guide.md` on GitHub, and confirm that each GIF plays and that the text matches the current plugin in Obsidian.\n\n## Issue\n\nCloses #13\n"
}